            <ArticleTitle>Intra-articular injections for joint disease in horses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>559-73, v</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lameness remains an important source of reduced performance in many types of horses. Pain referable to joints is among the most common causes, and intra-articular injections remain a common and important means of addressing lameness referable to joints in horses.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
